+`turn/*`, `step/*`, `user/message`, `assistant/*`, and `tool/*` are durable session events; the rest are live extension points across three domains. `agent/pre-step`, `agent/request`, `agent/request-layout`, `llm/stream`, and the three `tools/*` events are waterfalls, whose listeners must call `next()` to delegate; `agent/turn-stopping` is serial and has no `next()`.
 
 Input reaches the driver through one inbox. Some messages wake it immediately; injected context waits in the inbox until another message does.
 
 `agent/pre-step` decides what the model sees. Listeners may rewrite the claimed messages or reject them outright; a rejected or empty first claim still closes a durable turn that spent no step, so the log records the attempt. Each step reads the prompt sections and tool schemas that plugins registered.
 
+`agent/request-layout` receives the complete Session-derived message boundary after entered input and tool results are durable. Its default is identity; a listener may return another ordered message projection, while call configuration, system text, tools, request-header logging, freezing, and Provider dispatch remain loop-owned. The loop validates the projection and retains process-local source provenance for its invariant; a plugin whose projection depends on another durable source owns reconstruction from that source.
+
 Details: the [sequence diagram](agent-lifecycle.md), the [tool pipeline](tool-execution-pipeline.md), and [cancellation and error recovery](subsystems/core.md#the-agent-handle).
 
 ## Session log
 
-The session log is the source of the context the model sees. `deriveMessages()` projects model history from it, and raw `assistant/chunk` events preserve replay and UI fidelity. Fork, resume, transcripts, telemetry, and persistence all derive from this stream.
+The session log is the source of the local message boundary. `deriveMessages()` projects model history from it, and raw `assistant/chunk` events preserve replay and UI fidelity. Fork, resume, transcripts, telemetry, and persistence all derive from this stream.
 
-**Model-visible means logged.** Anything that reaches a model request must be reconstructable from the log, and a runtime invariant asserts it. This is why a new model-visible input requires a new session event: extend `SessionEventMap` and render from the log.
+**Model-visible means durably reconstructable.** Ordinary request content is reconstructed from the Session log, and a runtime invariant asserts its source boundary. A request-layout plugin may project that boundary only when it owns any additional durable inputs and reconstruction checks; process-local provenance does not replace that durability. New Session-owned model-visible input still requires a `SessionEventMap` event rendered by `deriveMessages()`.
 
