+<a id="agentrequest-layout--waterfall"></a>
+
+#### `agent/request-layout` — waterfall
+
+Replace only the ordered messages of one complete model request. The default result is `payload.messages`; listeners call `next()` to obtain and wrap the downstream projection. The loop validates message roles and tool-call/result ordering, then deep-freezes the final request before Provider dispatch. Configuration, system text, tools, Session history, and Provider invocation remain loop-owned.
+
+```ts cordis-catalog
+/**
+ * Replace only the ordered messages of one complete model request. The
+ * default result is `payload.messages`; listeners call `next()` to obtain
+ * and wrap the downstream projection. The loop validates message roles and
+ * tool-call/result ordering, then deep-freezes the final request before
+ * Provider dispatch. Configuration, system text, tools, Session history,
+ * and Provider invocation remain loop-owned.
+ * @param payload.agent - the agent making the model call.
+ * @param payload.sessionId - the durable Session identity stamped on the request.
+ * @param payload.turn - the open turn number.
+ * @param payload.step - the open step number.
+ * @param payload.attempt - one-based Provider attempt within this step; a new step resets it to one.
+ * @param payload.config - the effective request configuration recorded by the request header.
+ * @param payload.system - the rendered system prompt, when non-empty.
+ * @param payload.tools - the complete immutable tool-schema list.
+ * @param payload.messages - the complete immutable Session-derived messages before projection.
+ * @param payload.signal - the current turn's explicit abort signal.
+ * Scope-filtered dispatch (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-scope`): agent-scoped listeners receive only that agent.
+ * @mode waterfall
+ */
+'agent/request-layout'(this: Scoped<Agent>, payload: RequestLayoutInput, next: () => Promise<RequestLayoutResult>): Promise<RequestLayoutResult>
+```
+
+Types: [Scoped](scope.md)
